commit 15933868
author: cdvankammen
date: 2026-10-22 13:46:38 -0600
subject: fix(settings): sequential partial PATCHes no longer clobber each other

BUG (audit-found): updateSettings merged nested config keys against DEFAULTS
instead of the STORED value — a second partial PATCH (e.g.
{smartRouter:{allowedModels:[...]}}) reset the first PATCH's {enabled:true}
back to default false. UI was safe (sends full objects) but external API
partial PATCHes silently lost data.

Fix: split nested keys into CONFIG_MERGE_KEYS (accumulate against stored:
smartRouter, capacityAdapter, srComboCleanup) and MAP_REPLACE_KEYS (replace
semantics: modelFallbacks, *Strategies, quotaVisibility, dnsToolEnabled).
Read path unchanged (fills missing keys from defaults).

Tests: +2 (sequential smartRouter + capacityAdapter accumulation); 8/8 pass.


